You are working on the Enterprise Refinery AI Platform — a single-tenant RAG system for refinery operations.

## Stack (locked)
- Next.js 14 App Router + API Routes (full Node.js in Docker)
- Supabase PostgreSQL + pgvector
- Elasticsearch 8 (Docker)
- Supabase Auth + Resend
- Ollama llama3.2:3b (local LLM)
- Anthropic Claude API (cloud LLM)
- Google Gemini Vision (OCR)
- Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- TypeScript everywhere

## Rules
- No `any` types. No implicit types.
- No comments unless WHY is non-obvious.
- No mock databases in tests — use real Supabase test project.
- Unit tests colocated: `lib/rag/chunker.ts` → `lib/rag/chunker.test.ts`
- E2E tests in `/e2e` using Playwright.
- RBAC enforced at API route level, not just UI.
- PII scan before every cloud LLM call — mandatory, never skip.
- All LLM calls logged: model, tokens, latency, cache hit/miss.
- Stream LLM responses — never buffer full response before sending.
- No abstractions beyond current task requirements.
- No multi-tenancy — single tenant by design.
- No paid infra suggestions — free-tier demo.

## Folder Structure
- `apps/web/app/` — pages + layouts
- `apps/web/app/api/` — API routes
- `apps/web/lib/` — agents, rag, llm, ocr, db, search, auth
- `apps/web/components/` — React components
- `infra/docker/` — Docker Compose
- `infra/supabase/migrations/` — DB migrations
- `e2e/` — Playwright tests

## SDLC Phase
Analytics/PRD → Design → Development → Testing → Deployment
Current: Analytics / PRD
